; claude: Pascal (Niklaus Wirth, 1970) compiled to P-code and run on a
; P-machine, the scheme of Wirth's Pascal-P (1973) and of UCSD Pascal
; (1977): Pascal_lexer (the text to tokens), Pascal_compile (one pass
; of recursive descent that checks the types and emits the code as it
; reads, with no tree), Pcode (the stack machine's instructions, and a
; disassembler), Pmachine (the machine: its stack of frames, static
; links, run as a Talk conversation so that readln waits for a line
; and a long loop runs a slice a frame; or paused from outside, the
; debugger's), Pdebug (a paused machine read as Pascal: frames, links,
; watches, steps) and Pascal_disk (programs of the classics: Wirth's
; eight queens, the towers of Hanoi). For
; TinyTurboPascal (apps/devtools/, appkits/editor's Tui_turbo;
; plan_terminal.md, section 6).
;
; Pure OCaml, no Playground (libs/languages/README.md). A private
; library, installed as part of elm_playground.
(library
 (name pascal)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries terminal) ; Talk
)
